.TH PSReluDerivative 3 2025-01-20 "PsyC 0.9.5" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
\fBPSReluDerivative\fR \- Derivative of the ReLU activation function

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/activation.h>

.I
void  
.br
\fBPSReluDerivative\fR(\fIPSFloat *vec\fR, \fIPSFloat *dest\fR, \fIlong len\fR, \fIint acceleration\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Computes the derivative of ReLU activation function (\fIPSRelu\fR) for vectors.
.br
The derivative is computed on vector \fIvec\fR of length \fIlen\fR and stored into vector \fIdest\fR.
.br
If \fIdest\fR is \fINULL\fR, results will be stored into \fIvec\fR itself.
.br
For the \fIacceleration\fR argument, take a look at \fIPSAcceleration\fR.
.br
The equivalent function to be used with scalars is \fIPSReluDerivativeS\fR.

.SH SEE ALSO
psyc(1), PSRelu(3), PSReluDerivativeS(3)
